<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">General Maritime Treaty of 1820</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1820">1820</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The General Maritime Treaty of 1820 was signed between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the sheikhs of the coast of the lower Gulf after a British expedition destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qasimi">Qawasim</a> fleet at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras-al-khaimah">Ras al-Khaimah</a> in 1819. The rulers bound themselves to give up piracy and plunder at sea. It began British supremacy over what became the Trucial Coast, later strengthened by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/perpetual-maritime-truce">Perpetual Maritime Truce</a> of 1853 and the protection treaties of 1892.</p></div>
